/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (CBPMs are unlicensed \(specials\) schedule 2 Controlled Drugs. By law, they must be initiated exclusively by a consultant on the GMC Specialist Register, only when there is a clinically unmet need. While Pharmacist Independent Prescribers \(IPs\) cannot prescribe these unlicensed specials autonomously, they play a vital role within a delegated shared-care framework. They can work under the direction of the initiating specialist to manage patient titration, adjust dosages, and provide safety monitoring crucial for these complex treatment pathways.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
